            0.745,
            0.252
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "small intestine. The large intestine absorbs water and some salts from the undigested food, thus making the waste semi-solid. This semi-solid waste is called "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "stool",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": ". The stool is then stored in the lower part of the large intestine, called the "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "rectum",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": ", until the body is ready to get rid of it. Eating fibre-rich foods like fruits, vegetables, and whole grains helps the large intestine function properly by making the stool easier to pass. Finally, it is expelled through the anus—a process known as "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "egestion",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": ". This is how your body removes the waste it does not need, keeping you healthy!"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.252,
            0.744,
            0.291
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Isn’t it fascinating how the digestive system works, absorbing nutrients from food and eliminating waste?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.324,
            0.339,
            0.344
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "FASCINATING FACTS"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.349,
            0.729,
            0.482
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The large intestine contains various small living organisms, such as bacteria, that help in digestion. They help in keeping our digestive system healthy. They break down undigested food, especially fibre, and produce essential nutrients. Fibre-rich food, and especially ‘fermented foods’ (like curd, buttermilk, shrikhand, kanji, pickles, gundruk, and poita bhat) are good for a healthy digestive system and overall well-being."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
