        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.2,
            0.565,
            0.816,
            0.687
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The importance of digestion in maintaining good health has been recognised for centuries. The Charaka Samhita, an ancient Ayurvedic text, highlights the role of easily digestible foods and the judicious use of spices like ginger, black pepper, and cumin to enhance digestion. Advances in science in the area of nutrition also emphasise eating meals at proper timings, practising mindful eating, and avoiding overeating as key factors in maintaining digestive health."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.723,
            0.741,
            0.768
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "9.1.2 Do all animals digest food the same way as humans do?"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.202,
            0.797,
            0.511,
            0.868
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "I have seen cows keep chewing the food even when they are not actively grazing or eating anything. Why?"
            }
          ]
        },
